  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday through next Tuesday)\nIssued at 234 PM CDT Wed Sep 30 2026\n\nFriday will be our coolest day as the post frontal airmass will be\nin place. This will put highs across the Panhandles in the 60s to\nlower 70s. Saturday will be one of the coolest mornings we've seen\nin awhile with lows in the 40s to lower 50s. High pressure will\nrebuild over the Panhandles for the remainder of the extended with\na gradual warming trend so that we should be back in the upper 70s\nto lower 80s by Tuesday afternoon. There is a hint at a subtle\nwave in the northwest flow on Tuesday that could bring another\nround of showers and storms to the Panhandles, but otherwise the\nextended looks mostly mild and dry. \n\nWeber",
